WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.644
Local model serving is not automatically safe just because it runs nearby.

00:00:04.644 --> 00:00:09.566
Operators should understand what address the service listens on, who can reach it,

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:12.595
and which applications are expected to use it.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:17.139
A service intended for one user on a local machine has different

00:00:17.139 --> 00:00:20.168
risk than a service reachable by a team,

00:00:20.168 --> 00:00:22.819
a lab network, or other internal systems.

00:00:22.819 --> 00:00:25.848
Network exposure should be a deliberate architecture decision.

00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:31.149
If a model service is reachable by other hosts, teams may need authentication, authorization,

00:00:31.149 --> 00:00:34.178
firewalling, reverse proxy controls, monitoring, and documented ownership.

00:00:34.178 --> 00:00:38.722
The exact controls depend on the environment, but the principle is consistent:

00:00:38.722 --> 00:00:42.887
do not assume that being internal means access is automatically appropriate.

00:00:42.887 --> 00:00:45.916
Data handling is also part of security operations.

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:50.081
Prompts, retrieved context, file contents, and outputs may contain secrets, credentials,

00:00:50.081 --> 00:00:53.867
personal data, internal plans, customer information, or confidential work product.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:59.547
Integrations should avoid logging sensitive prompts or outputs unless a governed process explicitly requires it.

00:00:59.547 --> 00:01:04.848
When logs are necessary, teams should consider redaction, retention, and who can read them.

00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:08.256
Defensive operation focuses on clear access boundaries, privacy-aware logging,

00:01:08.256 --> 00:01:09.392
and supportable ownership.

00:01:09.392 --> 00:01:12.042
Operators should know which workflows are approved,

00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:16.964
which users or applications can reach the service, what data classes are allowed,

00:01:16.964 --> 00:01:18.479
and who reviews changes.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.780
These choices keep local AI useful without turning it into an unmanaged internal endpoint.
